@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Features";
}

<div class="container mt-5 mb-5">
    <h1 class="mb-4">Ohrbob Features</h1>
    <p class="lead">Ohrbob is a multi-platform app built in Avalonia that runs on Android, Linux, Windows (Mac and iOS planned). It is fully open-source, makes heavy use of C# and .NET, and consumes the podcast API from PodcastIndex.</p>
    
    <div class="row mt-5">
        <div class="col-md-6 mb-4">
            <h3><i class="bi bi-search text-primary"></i> Discover Podcasts</h3>
            <p class="text-muted">Easily search and discover new podcasts using the extensive, open PodcastIndex directory right from within the app.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 mb-4">
            <h3><i class="bi bi-plus-circle text-primary"></i> Add Manually</h3>
            <p class="text-muted">Have a private, premium, or unlisted podcast? Add it manually by simply pasting the RSS feed URI into your station.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 mb-4">
            <h3><i class="bi bi-sort-down text-primary"></i> Adjust Play Order and Span</h3>
            <p class="text-muted">Customize the order of your episodes (newest first, oldest first) and define the span. You can choose to keep only the last 5 episodes, or everything from the last 30 days. Perfect for staying up-to-date or binge-listening a backlog.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 mb-4">
            <h3><i class="bi bi-collection-play text-primary"></i> Group into Stations</h3>
            <p class="text-muted">Organize your podcasts into logical "Stations" (e.g., Daily News, Tech Talk, Comedy) for targeted, uninterrupted listening sessions.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 mb-4">
            <h3><i class="bi bi-sliders text-primary"></i> Station Configurations</h3>
            <ul class="text-muted">
                <li class="mb-2"><strong>Endless Spin:</strong> When your station runs out of new episodes, Endless Spin will automatically queue up older, unplayed episodes from your feeds so the audio never stops.</li>
                <li class="mb-2"><strong>Host Pace:</strong> Maintain a balanced mix of episodes from different feeds. Host Pace ensures one extremely prolific podcast doesn't dominate the station's entire playlist.</li>
                <li><strong>Aging Content:</strong> Keep your queue fresh by automatically dropping episodes that are too old or have been sitting unplayed for too long.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 mb-4">
            <h3><i class="bi bi-share text-primary"></i> Share Stations</h3>
            <p class="text-muted">Curated the perfect mix of morning news podcasts? Share your custom station setup with friends or the community so they can enjoy the exact same feed layout.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 mb-4">
            <h3><i class="bi bi-person-check text-primary"></i> Consistent Listening State</h3>
            <p class="text-muted">Your listening progress, playhead position, and history are synchronized securely to your profile. Start on your phone during a commute and seamlessly continue on your desktop.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 mb-4">
            <h3><i class="bi bi-filetype-xml text-primary"></i> Import OPML</h3>
            <p class="text-muted">Migrating from another podcast app? Import your existing podcast subscriptions in seconds using the industry-standard OPML format and sort them into stations later.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 mb-4">
            <h3><i class="bi bi-broadcast text-primary"></i> Streaming</h3>
            <p class="text-muted"><span class="badge bg-primary">Coming Soon</span> Stream episodes on-demand without having to wait for them to download completely to your device.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 mb-4">
            <h3><i class="bi bi-car-front text-primary"></i> Android Auto Support</h3>
            <p class="text-muted">Take your stations on the road. Ohrbob natively supports Android Auto, allowing you to control playback and browse your stations safely from your car's display.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
